WEBVTT

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.990
Federation police suspect that
the aim of the terrorist bombing

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.560
that took place in the Altan
district before dawn this morning

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.960
was to assassinate Bay Gelabu Bela,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.830
a Union consul general and
special ambassador for peace

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.800
who was paying a goodwill
visit to the Altan district.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.340
The investigation is ongoing.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.670
They say it was terrorists.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.660
Ugh! The world is so dangerous these days!

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.380
This is a very serious problem.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:38.480
We must not give the Union an
excuse to invade the neutral zone.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.980
What's the Union?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.020
They rule the half of the galaxy
that the Federation doesn't.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.590
Right now we're facing off over
control of the Beliosta neutral zone.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.590
May I have your attention?

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.990
Uh, yes, Sir!

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.500
This is footage captured by a
surveillance camera before the attack.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.330
He's an Ulgarian!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.340
You'll only be here for another two days.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.750
No further time was approved.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.080
It's enough.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.620
I'm grateful that I'm allowed to
participate in the investigation.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.450
Man, this place is sketchy...

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.680
Pretty much.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:29.070
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:38.060
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.080
<i>The sound of the battle raging somewhere</i>

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.050
<i>And the laughter right nearby</i>

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.990
<i>You can never hear it all</i>

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.590
<i>Because you have only one story</i>

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:59.500
<i>Only this sky sees all at</i>
<i>once the sorrow and smiles</i>

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.470
<i>That simultaneously fall in different</i>
<i>places around this wide world</i>

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:11.970
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:17.850
<i>How can it stay unchanging after</i>
<i>watching innumerable dramas?</i>

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>Even now everyone heads to his</i>
<i>own story without knowing a thing</i>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:32.320
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:43.460
<i>Wordlessly marking out</i>
<i>time longer than anyone's...</i>

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.160
The terrorist bombing has
turned the Altan district area

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.890
into an unrecognizable heap of rubble.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:06.360
Due to this, the body of Bay
Gelabu Bela hasn't yet been found,

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.800
but the probability of his survival
is regarded as almost zero.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.470
One Panglian milk soda.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.670
To ease tensions in the neutral zone,

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.660
chief consul Tirulu Gize has
expressed to the Union that...

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.710
Machuman is here!

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.700
- Oh, Machuman, save me!
- That's twelve palus. You pay in advance.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.990
FYI, I'm expensive.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:34.360
I don't find another Altan
around here too often. How much?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.260
What about that guy?

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.690
You interested, Boila?

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.760
I-I hate Altan women! They stink!

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.570
Now that's harsh.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.170
H-Hey!

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.270
I'm really good, you know!

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.570
- Tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle...
- Oh, you are good!

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:54.440
Say, you were in the Altan
district yesterday, weren't you?

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.850
I-I'm impressed you know that!

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.080
I liked you at first sight.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.120
So, what were you doing there?

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.920
I-I can't tell you that!

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.620
Oh, I see.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.290
Don't stop, please!

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.900
No more for you unless you tell me!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.760
W-Well...

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.200
Well?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.570
You're no ordinary hooker, are you?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:25.980
That gun's a Benoga blaster.
It's illegal for civilians to possess those.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.580
Maybe it would be easiest
to arrest you in the act now?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.980
You're a cop?!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.720
What the hell was that for?!

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.130
All-Powerful Staff!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.560
Please stop! I've gotta
keep a permit for this place!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.660
They're getting away!

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.060
Out of my way!

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.480
I think we've lost her...

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.460
Found you!

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.620
You're under arrest for
possession of illegal firearms,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:09.350
and you never answered my question!

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.350
Th-That's true...

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.340
W-Well, then!

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.030
Let's p-pick up where we l-left off!

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.100
Wedola! Help me!

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.980
As usual, you're not on your guard.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.610
Nechla!

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.520
How could you do that?!

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.020
Shouldn't I have?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.050
Obviously it's not okay to kill him!

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:45.720
Then what should I have done?

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.890
Bring him in alive!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.130
You understand nothing.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.120
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.560
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.470
Let me go, Musclewoman!

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.300
Then you cut it out, you psycho killer!

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.740
What's this stuff?!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.150
Hi, Wedola!

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.140
You really saved me, Nimukay!

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.350
They got away...

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.030
I don't understand this at all!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.840
If that pontiff hadn't interfered,
I could've arrested the suspect!

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.410
Why did she?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.340
Pontiffs work directly
under the Sanctum Sanctorum.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.280
The law can't touch them.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:45.180
Plus, she has special powers.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:45.380
She has superpowers?!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.580
"Superpowers"

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.180
She has superpowers?!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:51.220
No! He means she has a license to kill.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.520
And she interfered with the investigation...

00:06:54.520 --> 00:07:00.060
We can safely assume this matter is
of interest to the Sanctum Sanctorum.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.930
Either way, we're back to square one now.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.470
Not necessarily. A few hours ago,

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.070
an organization calling itself the
"New World Order Revolutionary Front"

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.970
claimed responsibility for the bombing...

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:11.960
Weegie.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.120
Yo, Federation public servants.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.150
Are you working hard
wasting the taxpayers' money?

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:27.460
Hi there, I'm Commander Kinzel of the
New World Order Revolutionary Front!

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.060
Kinzel?!
The just acts the Front recently took in the
Altan district were our great warning to you!

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:34.100
Yes. Kinzel Hower, the man you
and Nechla apprehended at El Kazan.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.460
He's an intellectual who
graduated from Milaton University

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.230
But the incompetent Federation
government has lost all racial pride

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:41.970
and a vicious terrorist who even
committed cannibalism on Planet Eon.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:42.740
It seems they don't understand
the true meaning of this warning!

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.740
He broke out of the Atola
satellite prison six months ago.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:46.840
It seems they don't understand
the true meaning of this warning!

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.610
So we've decided to give you
ladies and gents <i>another</i> warning!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:56.610
In twelve hours, we'll bring down the
hammer on that dirty Union consulate general!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:04.330
But since I'm such a merciful guy,
I think I'll give you one last chance.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:11.330
If you meet our demands, we are
prepared to call off this completely just act.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:16.170
We appoint these two to be the negotiators!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.840
Just you <i>watch:</i> those two will
brazenly walk in here to negotiate!

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:25.480
I had to eat smelly food because of those she-cats!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:31.220
I'll never, ever forgive those bitches!

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.890
- There, there...
- Oh, that's good!

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:39.300
By the way, who is this person
who's always giving us financial support?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:43.170
Yes, Sir, please tell us!

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.900
Haven't the foggiest!
But he understands my revolution,

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:51.310
so he's obviously a good guy
who graduated from college.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:55.210
And this job is a special request from our sponsor.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.880
Yeah, we're going to blow
up the Union consulate, right?

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.350
Oh, that's a bluff.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.550
Get a load of <i>this:</i>

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:07.320
our next target is the very
nest of all those computer people!

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.690
Huh? So you mean the Sanctum Sanctorum?

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.060
College graduates really know how to go all-out!

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:17.100
After all, these fireworks are
gonna be big as an antimatter bomb!

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.530
Boom!

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:31.180
Are you settled in with the mobile security police?

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.350
It's an active unit! At my age!

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:37.590
Why not? You're not suited to desk work.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.560
More importantly, it looks like
the Union is assembling a fleet

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:44.590
over the Beliosta neutral zone.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:47.130
Is there going to be war?!

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:51.570
We're doing our best to prevent that, Weegie.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:56.210
It's one reason we have to
catch Kinzel as soon as possible.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.610
I'm ashamed to be
the same species as him.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.240
But Kinzel is a pseudo-ideologue.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.410
Do you think he planned this all by himself?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.410
Are you onto something, Skeletso?

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:12.920
Oh, hey, I hear those two are teaming up again?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.960
Why do I have to work with <i>her?</i>
And on the Kinzel case again, too?!

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.660
Kinzel, eh? Maybe we've all
got some sort of karmic bond.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.800
You've got to be joking!

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:24.730
Yes, I am.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:26.100
Why, you...

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.090
Whoa, she knows how to joke?

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:35.280
Are you from here?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.410
No.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:41.780
Ever since I can remember,
it was Violin who raised me.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.780
A childcare marionette...

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:49.260
I see, so she was your substitute mother.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.530
Violin?

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.520
You mean that...

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.440
Where are we?

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.840
A mass burial site for us Altans.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:14.320
Kinzel! Birdy Cephon and party have
come to negotiate just like you asked!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.550
Show yourself!

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:19.690
We've been in this situation before.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:21.680
You mean it's like El Kazan?

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:25.720
This guy's stuck in a rut.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.220
Hey!

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.570
You see 'em?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:38.560
Nope!

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.080
Look at this wreckage.
There's no way they survived.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.070
Nope. Serves them right.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.350
Huh?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.180
What's this? An Altan brat?

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.160
What do we do?

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:59.150
He saw us. Take care of him.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.900
Wait!

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.870
You can't! He's just a kid!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.270
Please, darling, don't kill him!

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:12.240
Please...

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:15.870
What if we hold him in our
hideout until we've finished the job?

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.180
Jeez, fine. Whatever.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.070
Where am I?

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.870
Birdy? Birdy!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.860
She's not answering, huh?

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:57.080
Heh, I never would've
guessed you were our sponsor!

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.830
You played dead, eh?
I have to admit, I'm impressed...

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.400
...Mr. Consul General Gelabu.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.400
Enough idle chatter, Kinzel Hower.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:14.230
You just need to do what I told you to.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.110
Look at this.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:22.080
It's an abandoned electricity
satellite in geostationary orbit

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:25.350
10,000 myules above the capital.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:28.580
I'm going to crash it into the Sanctum Sanctorum.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:34.620
The plan is to crush everything in a 40-myule radius.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.610
Beginning satellite drop.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:47.970
Current <i>altitude:</i> 8000. Angle of <i>approach:</i> 75.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.370
Error <i>correction:</i> 25 pectars.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.340
Currently descending along predicted course.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:56.010
What now? What should I do, Birdy?!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:59.210
I don't mind quitting now, if you like.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:02.480
I mean, hey, if I press this button,
the satellite will self-destruct!

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.880
Kinzel!

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:12.230
I'm joking, I'm joking!
You Union types have no sense of humor.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:15.160
Tsutomu, is that the controller?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.500
Birdy?!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.500
My fleet will advance into
the neutral zone's airspace

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.700
as soon as the Sanctum Sanctorum is destroyed,

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:25.700
and regain our lost territory with
their overwhelming military force.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.250
I, the special ambassador for peace,
have been assassinated by the Federation!

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:36.750
With this pretext to act upon,
our invasion will be justified.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.190
You're some ambassador for peace.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.490
Kid?

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.480
Er...

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.370
Y-You brat!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.270
Hold it right there! Give that back!

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:54.270
Whoa, there!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.100
W-Wait! Um...

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.740
Don't move a muscle, kid! I'm gonna eat you alive!

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:05.740
Hmm, I'm not so sure about that.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.220
That's!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.620
Nobody told me you were here!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.560
Give up, Kinzel Hower!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:23.190
Kinzel let an investigator in here?! That fool!

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:28.740
The Union's supposedly dead
consul general in a terrorist's hideout...

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:32.570
You make an interesting pair.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:35.040
You're!

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.880
Kinzel! Where are you?!

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:49.260
Surprised? Behold the masterpiece
I created in college, the Amubis 777!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.260
He has the power of a heavy tank...

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.890
You oughta listen until I'm finished!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.600
That damned Kinzel... I can't believe
he's going to do a satellite drop.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.600
We've calculated the landing point.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.340
Their target seems to be the Sanctum Sanctorum.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:17.950
No use, no use, no use! This thing
has more power than you lxioran Altans.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.820
Never underestimate a college graduate!

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.260
Huh?

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:27.630
I told you to listen until I was finished!

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.830
O-Oh no!

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:48.450
Darling, what should I do with this?

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:51.020
Nimukay! Give that to me!

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:54.160
Distance to <i>target:</i> 60.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:58.360
Listen up! If that thing falls,
lots of innocent people will die!

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:01.200
Huh? Um... so about fifty?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.570
Don't listen to her!

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:04.970
More than that!

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.200
How many?

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.700
A lot!

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.910
What? A lot of people will die?!

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:14.880
I love you, my honey!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.580
I'm sorry!

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.080
Huh?

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.070
H-Hey!

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:29.190
Too bad. You were so close.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:33.860
I don't know what you mean, Pontiff.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.900
My fleet will advance into
the neutral zone's airspace

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.070
as soon as the Sanctum Sanctorum is destroyed,

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:43.770
and regain our lost territory with
their overwhelming military force.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.670
This is what she means.

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:50.680
l-lf that's made public, the Union will!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:55.280
I see, is <i>that</i> what you're doing here, Pontiff?!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.120
Your understanding will certainly expedite matters.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:03.230
That's what my country...
what the Union government wants, then?

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:08.900
Your Excellency's brave actions
shall surely benefit both governments.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:11.300
I know how to conduct myself!

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:19.040
I shall prove the justice of
the Union with my own blood!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.650
A political settlement, eh? Now all that's left is...

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:28.550
Wh-Why, you!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.450
But... But!

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.280
You bitch!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:48.240
I won't... I won't go down
in a place like this, dammit!

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:51.310
Okay, where's the scrawny dog?!

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:52.740
Over there.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:58.480
I graduated from college!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.320
Thanks to you, Kinzel and his men

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.250
have been safely confined
to the Atola satellite prison.

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:09.260
And when the Union received notice
of Gelabu's death in the line of duty,

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:11.190
they withdrew their criticisms.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.800
We've averted what could
have been an explosive situation.

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:17.170
It's what you'd call a political settlement.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:22.870
But I don't understand. I was
unconscious and couldn't contact you...

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.670
How did you locate their hideout?

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:28.510
I'll answer that question.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:32.950
Hey! It's you!

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:37.450
Let me introduce you.
This is our undercover investigator...

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.790
Kashu Geeze.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.560
Huh? Huh?!

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:44.230
He's also a subordinate of Skeletso's.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:47.500
Not that <i>I knew anything about it either...</i>

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:51.500
Forgive me. It was a covert operation.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.640
I'm a student of Instructor Skeletso's, too.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:58.210
You could call us fellow pupils.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.480
If you were doing an
undercover investigation of them,

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.980
I assume you could have
prevented the original bombing.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:06.970
If I had acted differently,
we couldn't have exposed the Union's plot.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.420
Hey, Birdy, stop!

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:22.000
Don't misunderstand this.
He carried out his mission.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:25.270
At the cost of innocent lives?

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:28.700
In order to save even more lives.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.120
In order to save more lives, eh?

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:45.250
Heh, I guess that <i>was</i> out of character.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:48.420
I hear there are military spies at work too.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:52.260
We have to keep the Tragedy of Bilugeva
from happening again...

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:55.700
Let's put our faith in our daughter.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:08.380
Sheesh! Hurry up and answer!

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:09.580
Hello?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:10.950
Senkawa?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.620
Oh, yeah. There were family circumstances.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:18.890
Right. I was out of Tokyo for a while.

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:24.880
Sure, I'm okay. I'll be at
school tomorrow. See you then.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:28.600
Good work, Tsutomu.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.590
That was like a dream...

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:32.600
"Receiving Email/Text"

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.590
"Inbox" "Sayaka Nakasugi" "Party"
"I'll be having a party to celebrate my
recovery on Sunday. I'd really like you to come."

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.000
Like a dream.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.810
<i>Let's go! Have a good time!</i>

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:46.980
<i>A peaceful, happy</i>
<i>cheek-to-cheek time for everybody</i>

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:52.980
<i>Put your hands, let's become one now</i>

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:01.260
<i>Come on, make some noise,</i>
<i>clap your hands, slap slap!</i>

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.330
<i>Lift your hands, clap your hands, slap slap!</i>

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.430
<i>Everyone has their worries</i>

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:07.700
<i>Given they're neverending,</i>
<i>what'll you do from here on out?</i>

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.610
<i>Live out the tight days</i>
<i>without getting upset about it</i>

00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:14.280
<i>Am I right, or am I right?</i>

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.280
<i>Everybody in the audience, lift your hands</i>

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:20.150
<i>Don't cry anymore; come on, lift your head</i>

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>And show us your smile, okay?</i>

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:28.890
<i>Right now we're gonna forget all</i>
<i>about the hard, painful, and sad stuff</i>

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:33.130
<i>C'mon baby, c'mon baby, everybody yeah yeah</i>

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:34.830
<i>Let's go! Have a new time!</i>

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:37.670
<i>Everybody give your best</i>
<i>good smile with all you've got</i>

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:41.570
<i>Happy smile, everything'll become one now</i>

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:43.200
<i>Let's go! Have a new world!</i>

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.470
<i>Don't worry, I won't let go of your hand</i>

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:50.250
<i>I know it'll help you get through the future</i>

00:22:50.250 --> 00:22:51.710
<i>Let's go! Have a good time!</i>

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:54.880
<i>A peaceful, happy</i>
<i>cheek-to-cheek time for everybody</i>

00:22:54.880 --> 00:22:58.890
<i>Put your hands, let's become one now</i>

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:00.220
<i>Let's go! Have a good time!</i>

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:03.690
<i>A peaceful, happy</i>
<i>cheek-to-cheek time for everybody</i>

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:09.320
<i>Put your hands, let's become one now</i>

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.400
<i>Shion Arita here, yessiree!</i>

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:19.540
<i>Tsutomu was invited to Nakasugi's party,</i>
<i>and his little heart's aflutter!</i>

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.440
<i>He's such an innocent!</i>

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:25.910
<i>But Birdy has a job:</i>
<i>to look for the Ryunka, yessiree!</i>

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:28.720
<i>Tsutomu is scared!</i>

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:33.790
<i>But if he gets to see Nakasugi,</i>
<i>he gets super-happy, Sirs!</i>

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:35.190
<i>What a simple guy!</i>

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.790
<i>Boys are even dumber than me, yessiree!</i>
